      "content": "**Getting Started with CloudScale DataStream API**\n\n**Overview**\nCloudScale DataStream API is a powerful tool for building scalable and efficient data pipelines. This guide will walk you through the key concepts and features to get you started.\n\n**Prerequisites**\nBefore you begin, make sure you have the following:\n\n* A CloudScale account\n* Familiarity with CloudScale's API architecture\n* A basic understanding of data streaming concepts\n\n**Setting Up Your Environment**\nTo get started, follow these steps:\n\n1. Install the CloudScale CLI tool using the following command: `cloudscale install cli`\n2. Configure your CloudScale account by running `cloudscale config`\n3. Create a new project using `cloudscale create project <project-name>`\n\n**Creating a DataStream**\nTo create a new DataStream, run the following command: `cloudscale create data-stream <data-stream-name>`\n\nThis will create a new DataStream with the specified name. You can then use the `cloudscale data-stream` command to manage and monitor your DataStream.\n\n**Next Steps**\nIn the following sections, we'll dive deeper into the features and capabilities of CloudScale DataStream API. We'll cover topics such as data ingestion, processing, and",
