      "content": "**Getting Started with CloudScale DataStream API**\n\n**Overview**\nCloudScale DataStream API is a powerful tool for building scalable and efficient data pipelines. This guide will walk you through the key concepts and features to get you started.\n\n**Prerequisites**\nBefore you begin, make sure you have the following:\n\n* A CloudScale account\n* Familiarity with CloudScale's API architecture\n* A basic understanding of data streaming concepts\n\n**Setting Up Your Environment**\nTo get started, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Install the CloudScale CLI tool**: Run the following command to install the CloudScale CLI tool: `cloudscale install cli --version 1.2.3 --build-time-flags \"-Dcloudscale.use-aws-iam-role=true\"`. This will install the latest version of the CLI tool with the necessary flags to use AWS IAM roles.\n2. **Configure your CloudScale account**: Run the following command to configure your CloudScale account: `cloudscale config --region us-west-2 --output-format json`. This will configure your account to use the US West 2 region and output the configuration in JSON format.\n3. **Create a new project**: You can create a new project using one of the following methods",
